I have:

`option_as_alt: Both`

and

  - { key: Key8,      mods: Alt,            chars: "\x5B"                    }
  - { key: Key9,      mods: Alt,            chars: "\x5D"                    }
  - { key: Key2,      mods: Alt,            chars: "\x40"                    }
  - { key: Key8,      mods: Alt|Shift,      chars: "\x7B"                    }
  - { key: Key9,      mods: Alt|Shift,      chars: "\x7D"                    }


and I can't type those chars! It's the same problem I had before and report it in #2280 and the solution (for me ans several others like you can see on the issue) was to change to:
`
alt_send_esc = false`

in emacs everything is working well unless the chars [  ]  {  }

I attach my alacritty.yml and an event log where I tried to type those chars (hope It's not full of garbage ...)

[files.zip](https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty/files/10778657/files.zip)

@reporter Ah, I see. Your bindings are incorrect, I'd suggest to run with `alacritty --print-events` and rebind the keys. So instead of:

```
- { key: Key8, mods: Alt, chars: "\x5B" }
```

you should do

```
- { key: LBracket, mods: Alt, chars: "\x5B" }
```

You can manually figure out what to bind via running with `alacritty --print-events | grep -i keyboardinput`. You can see `virtual_keycode` and rebind by it.
